## Art Deco and Geometric Settings in Practice

The Art Deco Fleur-De-Lis settings are the most direct expression of The Art Deco Rectangle Match. The fleur-de-lis arms frame the center stone with angular, symmetrical detail that echoes the radiant cut's rectangular outline.

The Diamond Filigree Vintage at $2,275 goes further — lace-pattern filigree under the head that reads as genuinely antique. The Hand-Engraved Micropavé at $2,315 adds individually hand-engraved shank detail that cannot be replicated by machine — each ring is slightly different from the next.

What separates these settings from less expensive vintage-label options is the undergallery. Turn a vintage ring upside down — if you see plain metal under the head, it is a modern setting wearing vintage arms.

If you see engraving, filigree, or open lacework under the head, it is a true vintage design. This detail reads from every angle, not just the top view. A buyer who checks the undergallery before ordering avoids the most common vintage ring disappointment.

