## Expert Summary

A vintage radiant cut engagement ring works when two rules are applied before choosing any setting. The Milgrain Boundary says to verify milgrain beadwork on the setting edges before buying — without it, a setting labeled vintage is a modern ring with decorative arms. The Art Deco Rectangle Match says the radiant cut's rectangular shape aligns naturally with Art Deco geometric design, making Art Deco settings the strongest vintage pairing for a radiant center stone.

Within the certified market range, the Milgrain Lace Pavé in 14k white gold at $2,650 is the best single setting. Paired with a 1ct D-VVS1 lab radiant at $932, the combined ring is $3,582 — below the price of most natural solitaires without vintage detail.

For buyers who want a natural stone and a GIA certificate, the same setting with a 1ct G-VS2 natural at $2,318 brings the combined total to $4,968. Both combinations pass The Milgrain Boundary test and deliver The Art Deco Rectangle Match.

